# FastStore franceretail Test Repo

This is a VTEX FastStore project used as a **learning/testing environment**.
The user is William Jeanne, VTEX Solution Engineer, **not a developer** — explain changes in plain language before applying them.

The same setup will later be replicated on a separate `soliverdemo` repo for an actual prospect demo (s.Oliver, Mode/Beauté/Lifestyle sector). For now, this repo is the playground.

## Account & live preview

- VTEX account: `franceretail` (Bricolage/Outillage catalog — Bosch, etc.)
- Live: https://franceretail.vtex.app
- Repo: https://github.com/Willjeanne/faststore-franceretail
- Locale: fr-FR, EUR

## Learning scope (in priority order)

1. ProductCard override (badge, price, image, hover)
2. PLP override (ProductGrid + filters layout)
3. PDP override (ProductDetails section: gallery, title, price, BuyButton, description)
4. Global theme tokens (colors, typography, radii, shadows)

## Critical rules

- Use FastStore design tokens (`--fs-color-*`, `--fs-text-*`, `--fs-border-*`) — never hardcode values
- Target components via `[data-fs-*]` attributes for SCSS overrides
- Place overrides in `src/components/overrides/` and custom sections in `src/components/sections/`
- Prefix custom components with `Custom` (CustomProductCard, CustomBuyButton)
- Never modify `@faststore/core` directly
- Never override `__experimentalProductCard` or `SearchInput` without warning the user about Intelligent Search analytics impact
- Always work on a branch, never push directly to main
- Always answer in French

## Workflow

For each task: read related files → check VTEX docs via `vtex-developer` MCP if needed → present a 5-line plan and wait for OK → implement minimal changes → tell the user what to verify at `http://localhost:3000`.

